1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,165
Metals react with dilute acids to make a metal salt and hydrogen gas.

2
00:00:04,165 --> 00:00:09,816
The salt depends on the acid: hydrochloric acid makes chlorides, sulfuric acid makes sulfates,

3
00:00:09,816 --> 00:00:16,123
and nitric acid makes nitrates. Sodium and potassium react far too violently with acids to try in the lab!

4
00:00:17,182 --> 00:00:22,953
Magnesium fizzes vigorously in dilute hydrochloric acid, making magnesium chloride and hydrogen.

5
00:00:22,953 --> 00:00:26,404
Zinc reacts more slowly, and copper doesn't react at all.

6
00:00:26,404 --> 00:00:30,985
Even fizzy drinks are acidic, so aluminium cans need a plastic lining inside.

7
00:00:32,044 --> 00:00:35,852
Gold and silver don't react with dilute acids, water or oxygen.

8
00:00:35,852 --> 00:00:40,016
A substance that doesn't react with other substances is called inert.

9
00:00:40,016 --> 00:00:44,300
Sometimes reactions make a mixture of products, and only one is wanted.

10
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:49,297
The rest are impurities, which must be removed, for example from medicines and food.

11
00:00:50,357 --> 00:00:56,485
The same mass of four metal powders is added, in turn, to the same volume of dilute hydrochloric acid.

12
00:00:56,485 --> 00:00:58,448
The temperature rise is measured.

13
00:00:59,507 --> 00:01:05,992
Magnesium makes the acid 18 degrees warmer, zinc 6, iron 3 and copper does not change the temperature at all.

14
00:01:07,052 --> 00:01:12,763
Pause and decide: why can the temperature rise be used to put the metals in order of reactivity?
